  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Namaacha Wind Power Plant, through WorleyParsons Limited</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study to assess the technical and financial viability, as well as economic and social impact of a wind power plant of up to 120 megawatts in Namaacha District, Mozambique. The grantee is eleQtra (Mocambique), Limitada and the U.S. firm WorleyParsons Group Inc. will be undertaking the feasibility study. This will be among Mozambique&apos;s first utility-scale wind power plants, thus helping to demonstrate the cost and performance of wind energy for the country, as well as improving access to electricity in Mozambique.</narrative>
  </description>
